+# Glic Payload Optimization for Local LLMs
+
+## Problem Summary
+
+Chrome's Glic pipeline sends payloads designed for Google's Gemini API, which includes:
+- **Base64-encoded screenshots** (1-5MB per image)
+- **Full DOM/Accessibility trees** (30-50K tokens for complex pages)
+- **Performance traces and debug data** (megabytes of noise)
+
+Local text-only LLMs like Llama 3 70B **cannot process images** and will:
+1. Tokenize base64 as garbage characters (100K+ tokens per screenshot)
+2. Exceed context window limits (8K-128K tokens)
+3. Timeout or crash during inference
+
+## Solution: Middleware Sanitization
+
+The updated `serve.py` now includes automatic payload sanitization that:
+
+### ✅ Removes Binary Data
+- Screenshots (`screenshot`, `imageData`, `binaryPayload`, etc.)
+- Thumbnails and snapshots
+- Any base64-encoded strings >10KB
+
+### ✅ Simplifies DOM Data
+- Strips HTML tags from page content
+- Converts to plain text
+- Truncates to ~6K tokens (24K characters)
+
+### ✅ Preserves Critical Node IDs
+- `backend_node_id` - Primary identifier for Chrome DevTools Protocol
+- `ax_node_id` - Accessibility tree identifier
+- `element_id`, `target_id` - Action target identifiers
+- Element metadata: `role`, `name`, `value`, `text`, `label`
+
+### ✅ Adds Actor System Prompt
+Automatically injects instructions for the LLM to output actions in the correct format:
+```json
+{
+  "action": "click",
+  "target_id": 12345
+}
+```
+
+## Testing the Sanitization
+
+### 1. Monitor Payload Sizes
+The proxy now logs sanitization details to stdout:
+```
+[PAYLOAD SANITIZATION]
+  Original size: 2,458,392 bytes (2400.8 KB)
+  [SANITIZE] Removed binary field: screenshot (size: 2145678 chars)
+  [SANITIZE] Stripped HTML and truncated (original: 45892 -> 24000 chars)
+  Sanitized size: 156,234 bytes (152.6 KB)
+  Reduction: 2,302,158 bytes (93.6%)
+```
+
+### 2. Debug Individual Payloads
+Use the included debug script to analyze payloads:
+```bash
+# Capture a payload from Chrome's network tab and save as payload.json
+python3 debug_payload.py payload.json
+```
+
+This will show:
+- Total payload size
+- Top 20 largest fields
+- Identification of base64/HTML/binary data
+- Estimated token count
+- Warnings if exceeding context limits
+
+### 3. Test with Simple Page First
+Start with a minimal page to verify the pipeline works:
+```html
+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html>
+<body>
+  <button id="test-btn">Click Me</button>
+  <input id="test-input" type="text" placeholder="Type here">
+</body>
+</html>
+```
+
+Expected sanitized payload should be <50KB.
+
+### 4. Test with Complex SPA
+Try a real-world page (e.g., Gmail, GitHub) and verify:
+- Payload size stays under 200KB
+- No base64 screenshot data in logs
+- Node IDs are preserved in the response
+- LLM responds within reasonable time (<30 seconds for Llama 3 70B)
+
+## Expected Performance Improvements
+
+| Metric | Before | After |
+|--------|--------|-------|
+| Payload Size | 1-5 MB | 50-200 KB |
+| Token Count | 100K-500K | 5K-15K |
+| Inference Time | Timeout | 5-30 seconds |
+| Context Window Usage | 500%+ | 10-20% |
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### Still Getting Timeouts?
+1. Check proxy logs for sanitization output
+2. Verify no `[SANITIZE] Removed binary field` messages are missing
+3. Use `debug_payload.py` to inspect the actual payload
+4. Check Ollama logs: `docker logs -f ollama` or `journalctl -u ollama -f`
+
+### Node IDs Not Working?
+1. Verify `backend_node_id` fields are present in sanitized payload
+2. Check that the Actor system prompt was injected
+3. Test with a simple page first to isolate the issue
+
+### LLM Not Understanding Page Context?
+1. Verify HTML stripping is working (check logs)
+2. Ensure plain text content is readable
+3. Try increasing the truncation limit (currently 24K chars)
+
+## Advanced Configuration
+
+### Adjust Truncation Limits
+Edit `serve.py` line ~180:
+```python
+if len(stripped) > 24000:  # Change this value
+    stripped = stripped[:24000] + "... [TRUNCATED]"
+```
+
+### Preserve Additional Fields
+Edit `serve.py` line ~70 to add more preserved keys:
+```python
+preserved_keys = {
+    'backend_node_id', 'backendNodeId',
+    'your_custom_field',  # Add here
+    # ...
+}
+```
+
+### Disable Sanitization (for debugging)
+Comment out the sanitization call in `_proxy_openai_chat`:
+```python
